(ROADMAP M0 — list growth across the realloc boundary. A list literal is
 created with capacity 8, so the 9th append is the first that must grow the
 block, copy the data AND the tag region, and return the new pointer. That
 path once segfaulted on the 9th element; the sizes here bracket it at 9,
 100 and 100 000.

 Each check reads back the first and last element as well as the length, so
 a realloc that loses or misaligns the copied data fails rather than merely
 counting correctly.)

a list called nine is [].
a number called i is 1.
While i is less than or equal to 9,
  Append i to nine,
  Increment i.
print nine's length.
print element 1 of nine.
print element 9 of nine.

a list called hundred is [].
set i to 1.
While i is less than or equal to 100,
  Append i to hundred,
  Increment i.
print hundred's length.
print element 1 of hundred.
print element 100 of hundred.

a list called many is [].
set i to 1.
While i is less than or equal to 100000,
  Append i to many,
  Increment i.
print many's length.
print element 1 of many.
print element 100000 of many.
